<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zerbst</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zerbst is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. From 1603 to 1793 it was the residence of the princes of Anhalt-Zerbst, who built a large baroque palace there. Its best-known daughter of the house was Sophie Auguste Friederike, who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. The palace and much of the old town were destroyed in an air raid in April 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zerbst.jpg" alt="Zerbst" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: mazbln · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zerbst_Bartholom%C3%A4ikirche.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
